"""cos-flow: read-only facts about the data-org board for STEWARD's briefs (plan 2026-11-14, items 8 and 9). No model.

  cos-flow lanes    [--json]          lane counts as the Lanes view shows them (every item, by Status), plus open-only
  cos-flow week     [--days 7] [--json]   the throughput readout from GitHub's own lane-move history
                                      (ProjectV2ItemStatusChangedEvent): forward and backward moves, finishes, drops,
                                      median days in Defining and Shipping, cards in one lane past 14 days
  cos-flow evidence [--json]          "evidence says #N can move to <lane>" lines, each for its owner, each with a link
  cos-flow nostatus [--json]          open cards in No Status, for their owners
  cos-flow today    [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--json]   DRD/DADR facts on cards worked today (board activity and Agent
                                      Atlas recent work): the card's DRD line, drd/ and dadr/ on main, open doc PRs,
                                      and the structural signals of PR #524's four-row check
  cos-flow debt     [--json]          definition debt for the Friday brief
  cos-flow next-id  DRD|DADR <NNNN> [--head <branch>]   is this number still free? Runs make next-id, then checks
                                      every open PR (make next-id reads only the newest 30) and main. Exit 65 if taken.
  cos-flow brief    capture|week <out-dir>   writes the files a scheduled brief reads (flow-*.md and flow-*.json)

Read-only: GraphQL queries, gh pr list, git show of origin/main. It never moves a card, never comments, never edits.
Lanes move only through make set-pillar (Status) and finishes through make complete, by the person on the card or by
Cassidy on his own cards with the evidence cited (cos-run gh lane). Team numbers only: no sums per person.
COS_FLOW_FIXTURE=<file.json> replaces GitHub, git and Agent Atlas with a fixture (installer tests).
"""
